From 61975bfb28cd9e7732985ed398fd963e276eea1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: upstream's host tests follow the port's patches

ps3recomp's own tests, run on the patched tree, failed where the port changed a
design on purpose or added a call from a unit the tests compile on its own:

- test_spurs_coordinator_kick: the coordinator sleeps on its own condition
  variable (kwake, patch 1015), so the waiter sleeps there.
- test_spu_coherency (test_spu_context_registries): a store that ends a line's
  last reservation drops its mark (patch 0002); the old expectation holds with
  SPU_COH_KEEP_MARKS=1, and the test now checks both.
- The GCM fixtures that compile cellGcmSys.c in: the tracing spans (patches 2009, 3021)
  and the GPU MLAA call (patch 2036), from libs/video/tests/port_links.h;
  test_rsx_immediate_vertices links runtime/ps3_trace.c.
- test_sail_boot_callback, test_sysmodule_unload_module_ex: ppu_prof_stamp_host
  (patch 3014). test_mfc_resume_elements, test_spu_poison_scan: g_spu_dma_hook
  (patch 1012).
- test_lwcond_layout: the lwcond wait's host condition variable and its trace span
  (patches 3005, 3021).
- The SPU interpreter fixtures and test_spu_program_pipeline: spu_wrch is a
  function-like macro outside spu_channels.c (the inline MFC latch, patch
  1004), so a stub definition parenthesises the name.
